@*
    Idiomatic Heddle -- composed-page chrome fragments (phase 9; authoring standard D16).

    Patterns followed, from Heddle's own documentation:
      Language reference   docs/language-reference.md ("Composition without coupling" --
                           definition libraries imported via @<<, Q1.7)
      Architecture         docs/architecture.md

    Definition-only library: the page's inert literal text (alert banner, secondary menus,
    fixed asset/script fragments) as named definitions the layout calls at its composition
    points. Importing it renders nothing; any piece is overridable with <name:name>. All
    display text lives in templates -- the C# tier carries only model data (ledger E22).
*@
